      "key": "spec_drift_signal_interpretation",
      "statement": "Unowned requirements, ungrounded design records, unrecorded deferments, and code without trace authority are design drift. A design artifact without requirement grounding lacks constitutional authority; code without design ownership demonstrates drift; shipping code/tests lacking live requirement and design trace are ungoverned Product surface. Tests of implementation habit rather than requirement truth lock in drift. Persistent observation/projection delta requires intake diagnosis but alone establishes neither wrong relation nor observation sufficiency. Requirements/design without a capability scenario leave operational meaning unverified. Treating guarantees, governance rules, or verification obligations as features misclassifies requirements. In-place correction of live constitutional artifacts corrupts history. A realization patch cannot close a use-case gap whose required meaning is absent from current requirements: the governing gap remains unresolved, intake selects its owning layer, and missing requirement meaning alone establishes no direction/scope change.",
