      "key": "spec_migration_adoption",
      "statement": "Inherited constitutional documents become migration source, not new-line authority. Every retained statement, requirement, design choice, or guide rule requires explicit re-adoption; carry-forward is intentional and should land in goals, intent, product, requirements, design, guide, or template as appropriate. Absence means not yet adopted, with no inherited authority. Old design/code govern only if explicitly re-derived and re-adopted; a sideways reference line has no live implementation authority. Before reuse classify every inherited module, interface, carrier, projection, and proof surface: carry_across means materially unchanged and intentionally re-adopted; redundant means no longer needed; rewrite means needed but rebuilt under new requirements/design. Unclassified inherited implementation is a defect. The represented sequence declares the migration line; establishes fresh method/goals/intent/product/requirements/design surfaces; moves prior implementation sideways if needed; classifies constitutional material as adopted/superseded/deferred/orphaned and implementation as carry_across/redundant/rewrite; copies only intentional retentions; and re-derives downstream design/code from new surfaces. carry_across never means automatic copying. Direct runtime, projection, prompt, proof, or review dependence on the sideways line is bridge debt; partially target-like proxy interfaces still depending on it are not lawful closure. Creating a new surface is lawful supersession rather than violation of old-surface immutability.",
